# Exported *ForTest* seams in non-test Go code (#17342), checked by
# internal/fortestcensus (make go-fortest-seam-rule).
#
# The deadcode gate cannot see an uncalled EXPORTED method on a live type
# (docs/testing.md, "What the deadcode gate cannot see"), so every exported
# func or method whose name contains ForTest (ForTesting too) needs a row
# here: <package dir>.<Name> or <package dir>.(<Receiver>).<Name>, a TAB,
# and a one-line reason it is exported. A seam without a row fails; a row
# naming no such seam fails. Nothing counts callers: when a seam's last
# caller goes, delete the seam and its row in the same change (or unexport
# it, and the deadcode gate takes over).
#
# Seeded 2026-11-16 from today's tree as-is, with each reason derived from
# an exact `git grep` of its callers.
pkg/api.(Server).HTTPHandlerForTest	cross-package seam: called by tests in pkg/daemon
